# guidance: item tooltips (§4.7)
tooltip.ntm-it.server.column=Placed as a 3-cell column: the cell you place is the core, the two cells above it belong to the structure.
tooltip.ntm-it.server.right_click=Right-click for the control screen, sneak-right-click for a status readout.
tooltip.ntm-it.server.server_core.hint=Core unit: takes HE power on all six faces, runs the data classes and pays for them with heat.
tooltip.ntm-it.server.server_core.faces=Front faces you. Compute units go on the two side faces, the heat exchanger goes behind.
tooltip.ntm-it.server.server_compute.hint=Compute unit: adds compute points to the core it is attached to, and produces heat.
tooltip.ntm-it.server.server_compute.faces=Front faces you. It attaches to the core through its two side faces, and the heat exchanger goes behind it.
tooltip.ntm-it.server.server_heat_exchanger.hint=Heat exchanger: the unit that carries heat away. Put it next to a core or compute column and give it a fluid to boil.
tooltip.ntm-it.server.server_heat_exchanger.faces=Any of its four horizontal sides works; the back of a column is where the design expects it. Touching exchangers act as one array. Coolant goes in through one tank and comes out of the other.

